  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between nortriptyline and Sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) through a chain of side effects. Nortriptyline is associated with parotid swelling, which is a side effect of both cyclobenzaprine and trimipramine. Trimipramine, in turn, is linked to lymphadenitis, and both cyclobenzaprine and trimipramine are known to target SHBG. This indicates that the observed side effects may be mediated through common pathways involving SHBG, possibly through the modulation of neurotransmitter activity or inflammatory responses. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of support for this relationship, though the evidence is not definitive. The mechanism may involve the influence of nortriptyline on neurotransmitter systems that indirectly affect SHBG levels, though further research is needed to establish a direct causal link.",
